          "section": "3.1 Electron beam melting",
          "quote": "Additive manufacturing by PBF-EB was used to fabricate cuboidal samples of the Ni-base superalloy CMSX-4. The experiments were carried out on an Arcam A2 EBM system. The electron beam operated at 60 kV acceleration voltage under a 10^-3 mbar helium atmosphere.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "25cbccb63504f11a:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 5,
          "section": "3.1 Electron beam melting",
          "quote": "The distance between the scan lines (line offset) was set to 100 µm, and a height of 50 µm was chosen for the individual layers, resulting in an effective powder layer thickness of about 100 µm, considering powder consolidation. The build chamber temperature was kept at 1000 °C",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "25cbccb63504f11a:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
