      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "section": "4.3 Multi-layer simulations",
          "quote": "Before melting, the scan area was selectively preheated with a defocused electron beam for 2.5 s until it reached a temperature of 1246 °C, 100 °C lower than the melting temperature of CMSX-4. Because of this, a shallow temperature gradient should be achieved. Preheating is usually performed by rapid line order scanning, resulting in a nearly uniform heat input. The preheating was modeled using an effective area heat source, applying a power of 150 W evenly across the melting area of 7.5 mm × 7.5 mm.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
